an5.31:9.1 starts: Just as the moon, unblemished,
an5.31:9.2 starts: going through the property of space,
an5.31:9.3 starts: outshines through brightness
an5.31:9.4 starts: all the constellations in the cosmos,
an5.31:12.1 starts: just so does one consummate in vision,
an5.31:12.2 starts: a disciple of the rightly self-awakened one,
an5.31:12.3 starts: wise,
an5.31:12.4 starts: excel the miser in five ways—
an5.36:3.2 starts: their offering bears an abundance.
an5.36:3.3 starts: Those who rejoice in that gift
an5.36:3.4 starts: or give assistance,
an5.36:3.5 starts: they, too, have a share of the merit,
an5.36:3.6 starts: and the offering isn’t depleted by that.
an5.36:4.1 starts: So, with an unhesitant mind,
an5.36:4.2 starts: one should give where the gift bears great
an5.36:4.3 starts: Merit is what establishes
an5.36:4.4 starts: living beings in the next life.
an5.41:8.1 starts: For whatever aim a wise householder
an5.41:8.2 starts: would desire wealth,
an5.41:8.3 starts: that aim have I attained.
an5.41:8.4 starts: I have done what will not lead to
an5.57:16.1 starts: There’s now no way
an5.57:16.2 starts: I could partake of sensual pleasures.
an5.57:16.3 starts: Having followed the holy life,
an5.57:16.4 starts: I will not return.”
an5.179:8.1 starts: “Seeing the danger in hells,
an5.179:8.2 starts: the wise would shun evils,
an5.179:8.3 starts: would shun them,
an5.179:8.4 starts: taking on the noble Dhamma.
an5.31:11.1 starts: Just as a hundred-billowed,
an5.31:11.2 starts: lightning-garlanded,
an5.31:11.3 starts: raining down on the wealth-bearing [earth],
an5.31:11.4 starts: fills the highlands and low,
an5.38:6.1 starts: To him come those without effluent—
an5.38:6.2 starts: free from passion,
an5.38:6.3 starts: free from delusion—
an5.38:6.4 starts: the field of merit for the world.
an5.43:10.1 starts: the wise praise heedfulness
an5.43:10.2 starts: in making merit.
an5.43:10.3 starts: The wise person, heedful,
an5.43:10.4 starts: acquires a two-fold welfare:
an5.57:12.1 starts: “‘Subject to birth, subject to aging,
an5.57:12.2 starts: subject to death,
an5.57:12.3 starts: run-of-the-mill people
an5.57:12.4 starts: are repelled by those who suffer
an5.179:12.1 starts: When hoping for merit,
an5.179:12.2 starts: provide gifts first
an5.179:12.3 starts: to those peaceful ones, ideal,
an5.179:12.4 starts: to whom what is offered, given,
